1. Overview

TENTORA is an AI-powered creative-solutions platform designed to help project owners obtain creative work through two connected paths:

Design Now: select a ready interactive design, customize it through controlled properties and AI-assisted actions, then preview, save, or export the result.

Work With a Creative: select one or multiple services, complete one visual taste test, receive up to six compatible creative or team recommendations, select the preferred option, and manage the project through delivery.

The MVP is planned as a web application using React, Flask, and PostgreSQL. Implementation must follow the modular-monolith direction in Stage 3 unless an approved Architecture Decision Record changes it.

This document is a development and evidence plan. Statements must be updated with repository links, screenshots, pull requests, test results, and final status as implementation progresses. Planned items must not be reported as completed until they are verified.

2. MVP Development Objectives

The implementation stage aims to deliver and validate the following functional areas:

Five project-sector entry points.

Sector-specific creative services and curated work examples.

A clear choice between Design Now and Work With a Creative.

A limited Ready Design pilot with controlled editable properties.

At least one validated preview and export flow.

One approved AI-assisted customization action within the Ready Design rules.

One or multiple service selection through My Project Needs.

One Main Taste Profile per project.

Optional service-specific taste refinement without repeating the full test.

A curated Creative DNA dataset.

Explainable matching with no more than six creative or team recommendations.

Creative profiles and portfolio exploration.

Design-to-Creative handoff.

A basic project workspace for messages, files, milestones, feedback, and deliverables.

Progressive authentication that preserves anonymous progress.

