6. Agile Delivery Method

Development is proposed as four one-week sprints. The team must confirm capacity, ownership, and dependencies at kickoff; the four-week duration must not be presented as validated until that review is complete. Each sprint includes:

Sprint planning.

Task assignment.

Implementation on feature branches.

Continuous QA and issue reporting.

Pull request review.

Sprint demonstration.

Retrospective and backlog adjustment.

The four-sprint duration is a constraint. Features that threaten the core demonstration must be reduced or deferred according to Stage 2 scope rules.

6.1 Priority Method

The backlog uses MoSCoW priority:

Must Have: required for the connected MVP demonstration.

Should Have: important but can use a simplified fallback.

Could Have: implemented only if Must and Should items are stable.

Won't Have: explicitly deferred from the MVP.

