13. Local Development Environment

13.1 Backend

The Flask API runs locally during development. The exact port must be documented in the repository setup instructions.

Example:

http://localhost:5000

13.2 Frontend

The React development server runs locally using the configured project toolchain.

Example:

http://localhost:5173

13.3 Database

PostgreSQL runs locally or through an approved development container. Postico or another PostgreSQL client may be used for inspection, but schema changes must be made through migrations rather than manual production-style edits.

13.4 Storage and Processing

The MVP may begin with local development storage, but application code should use a storage interface so it can move to private object storage later. Exports and longer AI actions should use a background-worker interface when synchronous processing becomes unreliable.

14. Environment Variables and Secrets

Real secrets must never be committed to GitHub. Commit an .env.example file containing names and safe placeholders only.

Example categories:

FLASK_ENV=development
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/tentora
JWT_SECRET_KEY=replace-me
FRONTEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
STORAGE_BACKEND=local
STORAGE_PATH=./storage
AI_PROVIDER=disabled
AI_API_KEY=replace-me

The actual project may use different names. .env must be excluded through .gitignore.

